cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these data, please cite the article given as preferred citation and this repository."
title: "The Kerr metric in canonical harmonic coordinates: recursion and checks"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Sadu
    given-names: Amina
    affiliation: "Université Paris-Saclay, Orsay, France"
  - family-names: Vanhove
    given-names: Pierre
    affiliation: "Institut de Physique Théorique, Université Paris-Saclay, CEA, CNRS, Gif-sur-Yvette, France"
abstract: >-
  Position-space implementation, in exact rational arithmetic, of the
  perturbative recursion that reconstructs the Kerr metric in canonical
  harmonic coordinates, with the checks reported in the article and the coefficients
  of the expansion in Newton's constant and in the spin.
keywords:
  - general relativity
  - Kerr black hole
  - harmonic coordinates
  - post-Minkowskian expansion
  - scattering amplitudes
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "The Kerr Metric in Canonical Harmonic Coordinates to All Orders"
